WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 19 Student Video
Unit 5, Lesson 3: Diety

1
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.940
Growing up in a Christian home, I heard many sermons about Jesus being God.

2
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.460
I believed it and it always made sense to me.

3
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.200
But for some reason, I thought the evidence for it was just a few isolated passages,

4
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.960
maybe in the Gospel of John and a few in the letters of Paul.

5
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:23.320
As I got older and really started to own my own faith and study the Scriptures more

6
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:29.180
closely, I began to realize that the idea that Jesus is God is central to the entire

7
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.500
biblical narrative.

8
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.760
Years ago, I had a conversation with a friend of mine.

9
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.120
It was late one night in college and we were up talking about God and the afterlife

10
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.780
and religion. And he said something that for some reason at that point in my life

11
00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:56.140
stuck with me. He said, you know, of all the great world religious leaders,

12
00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:01.280
Jesus is the only one who claimed to be God in human flesh.

13
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.460
As I thought about it, I realized that he's right.

14
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.240
Other religious figures claimed to tell us how to get to God.

15
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.380
or how to find truth, but Jesus claimed to be God.

16
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:18.280
And he gave powerful evidence, fulfilled prophecy and miracles to back up that

17
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:18.600
claim.

18
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:25.600
Jesus said the most important question we can answer in life is related to his own

19
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:31.540
identity. In Mark 8:29, Jesus asked, Who do you say that I am?

20
00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.980
Muhammad certainly didn't claim to be God.

21
00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:39.460
He claimed to be a prophet who revealed the will of Allah.

22
00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.040
And Buddha didn't claim to be God either.

23
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.940
Buddha claimed to reveal the path to enlightenment.

24
00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.780
But Jesus, on the other hand, claimed to be divine.

25
00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.080
He claimed to be God in human flesh.

26
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.340
The Old Testament prepares the way for the coming of Jesus.

27
00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.880
Luke 24:27 says,

28
00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.820
in all the scriptures, the things concerning himself.

29
00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:15.460
Let me highlight just briefly the things that Jesus said and did to reveal

30
00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.860
that he is God.

31
00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:23.620
First, Jesus has the authority to forgive sins that were committed against God

32
00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:29.260
himself. In Mark chapter 2, a group of men bring a paralytic to Jesus

33
00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:35.020
and Jesus announces by his own authority that the man's sins are forgiven.

34
00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:40.500
Because the religious leaders believed that only God could forgive sins committed

35
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.800
against him, they accused Jesus of blasphemy but rather than backing down, Jesus

36
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:51.720
healed the paralytic demonstrating that he spoke with the authority of

37
00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:57.540
God. Second, Jesus allowed people to worship him, which was something only

38
00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:03.140
God was supposed to receive. After Jesus walked on water he got in the boat and

39
00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:09.080
Matthew 14:33 says that the disciples worshipped him saying truly you

40
00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:14.960
are the Son of God. If Jesus were not truly God he would have stopped the disciples

41
00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.100
and other people from worshiping him.

42
00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.180
In fact this is what we see happen in Scripture.

43
00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:24.240
In Acts 14 it describes how Paul and Barnabas are in Lystra and they perform a

44
00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:29.480
miracle and the people fall down to worship them but they stop and they say no

45
00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.900
don't worship us only worship God we see the same thing happen again in Revelation

46
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:40.700
19. John falls down to worship the angel and again the angel says

47
00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:46.360
do not worship me stop worship God alone and yet Jesus allowed

48
00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:52.220
people to worship him why because he understood himself as God in human

49
00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:56.980
flesh. Third, Jesus claimed the name of God.

50
00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.580
In John chapter 8 the religious leaders are critiquing Jesus because he claimed to

51
00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.020
have been around during the time of Abraham.

52
00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:08.300
They're saying wait a minute Abraham lived a couple thousand years ago and you're

53
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:14.080
not even 50 how can this be? Well in reminiscence of Exodus chapter 3 verse

54
00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:18.940
14 when God first appears and reveals himself to Moses.

55
00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:23.120
And Moses asks who he is. He says, I am who I am.

56
00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:29.220
Jesus turns and looks at the religious leaders and in John 8:58 he says,

57
00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:34.360
truly truly I say to you before Abraham was I am.

58
00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:40.300
And they pick up stones to kill him because by claiming this name Jesus was making

59
00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:46.160
himself out to be equal to God. Fourth, other people including

60
00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:51.140
inspired biblical writers referred to Jesus as God.

61
00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:56.960
Hebrews 1:8 says, but of the Son he says your throne O God

62
00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:02.840
is forever and ever. The author of Hebrews understood Jesus as the eternal

63
00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.240
God who reigns forever.

64
00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.980
And in Titus 2:13, the Apostle Paul, who had seen the risen Jesus,

65
00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:18.680
says the appearing of the glory of our great God and Savior, Jesus Christ.

66
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.700
The Apostle Paul understood Jesus to be both God and Savior.

67
00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:29.360
We've only considered a handful of examples, but the consistent narrative from the

68
00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.460
preparation in the Old Testament through the entirety of the New Testament is

69
00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.240
that Jesus was and is divine.

70
00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:47.860
Personally speaking, understanding that Jesus was and is God was a

71
00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.220
game changer. I began to realize this isn't just a secondary theological issue in

72
00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:56.900
the scriptures, but the heart of the scriptures is that God has revealed himself in

73
00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:02.200
Jesus Christ. And this needs to affect the way I live my life, how I spend my money,

74
00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:07.440
my time, use my body, my profession, everything should be geared towards following

75
00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:12.060
and submitting to and loving Jesus who is the Lord of the universe.

76
00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:18.340
So here's the question for you. Have you made a decision to be a follower of Jesus?

77
00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:22.200
I grew up in a Christian home and I heard the gospel a lot.

78
00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:26.580
Sometimes it was just words until I hit that point in my life where I realized that

79
00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.220
I too was a sinner and needed Jesus.

80
00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:34.300
Because the gospel basically says that God has created us in his image.

81
00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:39.800
He has a plan for our lives, but all of us have done certain wrong things and they

82
00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:45.720
separate us from a holy God. And the only way we can have salvation is if

83
00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:51.680
we put our faith and trust in Jesus Christ, God in human flesh who died

84
00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:57.640
on the cross for our sins and paid the price that we deserved so are

85
00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:03.520
you willing to turn from your sins and repent and trust and follow jesus

86
00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:09.400
if you do the bible says people in heaven rejoice and that you personally will

87
00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.460
have eternal life

